# Line-ending policy.
#
# The working tree had drifted to CRLF while HEAD stored LF, so every tracked
# file showed as modified even when untouched. These rules normalize the repo
# and stop it recurring.
#
#   text=auto  Git detects text vs binary and normalizes to LF on commit.
#   eol=lf     Text files are LF in the working tree too, on every platform.
#
# eol=lf is deliberate rather than leaving checkout platform-native: this repo
# ships a Makefile (tab-sensitive) and a Dockerfile (CRLF breaks RUN lines), and
# the project targets Linux/CUDA and macOS/MPS. Pinning LF everywhere keeps a
# Windows checkout from reintroducing the drift.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files where LF is a correctness requirement, not a preference.
Makefile       text eol=lf
Dockerfile     text eol=lf
*.sh           text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts. All are gitignored today, but declaring them means a stray
# commit is never corrupted by line-ending conversion.
*.safetensors  binary
*.bin          binary
*.pt           binary
*.ckpt         binary
*.npy          binary
*.png          binary
*.jpg          binary
*.jpeg         binary
*.gz           binary
*.zip          binary
